# M2_limitation_contraction_ML.xps -- runs M2_limitation_contraction_ML.ode in one go (the steps at the top of the .ode).
#   XPPAUT 8.4:  File > Do script > M2_limitation_contraction_ML.xps    (or: xppaut M2_limitation_contraction_ML.ode -script M2_limitation_contraction_ML.xps)
#   XPPAUT-Web:  pick it under Scripts (group iso-test), or open the link with ?script=
speed 0.3
msg "M2, backward integration with k = 3 periods: start on the straight isochron at gamma0, integrate back by (k - th) T"
keys v 2
ans X-axis=ve|Y-axis=we|Xmin=-70|Ymin=0.0|Xmax=50|Ymax=0.65|Xlabel=v|Ylabel=w
keys u c a
ans thc
ans c
ans 0
ans 1
keys esc
keys i 2
ans Vary1=u|Start1=-1|End1=1|Vary2=th|Start2=0|End2=0.9|Steps=80|Steps2=9|Reset storage (Y/N)=N|Use old ic's (Y/N)=Y|Cycle color (Y/N)=N|Movie(Y/N)=N|Crv(1) Array(2)=2
keys n n
msg "Window 1: each dot is the end of one backward run, coloured by its target phase th = 0, 0.1, ..., 0.9"
wait 4
keys m c
keys u c a
ans err
ans c
ans 0
ans 1
keys esc
keys v 2
ans X-axis=ve|Y-axis=we|Xmin=-70|Ymin=0.0|Xmax=50|Ymax=0.65|Xlabel=v|Ylabel=w
keys r
keys n n
msg "Done. M2's limitation: after 3 periods backward, the dots in colours other than red are not on their isochron, and many ran off. Backward integration magnifies errors by the contraction of Gamma."
